.staging/
log/
.env
*.prev

# Runtime state: durable on disk, deliberately not source. The browser profile is
# hundreds of megabytes of cache, screenshots are byproducts, and schedule.json is
# rewritten every time a job runs -- committing it would be a commit per minute.
# Nothing here is needed to run a fresh copy: it all regenerates.
data/

# Instance state, not source. These live in the program's own root because a
# stdlib-only harness has no other place to put them, and each one is created on
# demand: `claw setup` writes config.yml and Notes.ensure! creates the two notes
# files, so a fresh clone needs none of them. Committing them shipped one
# machine's endpoint, and one instance's own accumulated notes, to everyone.
memory.md
preferences.md
config.yml
